## Guest Hooks

- `onBeforeGuestPasswordResetRequest`

{% aside type="caution" %}
`onBeforeGuestPublicTicketOpen`, `onAfterGuestPublicTicketOpen`, `onAfterGuestPublicTicketClose`, and `onAfterGuestPublicTicketReply` were removed in 0.8.3. Guest tickets now fire the client ticket hooks (`onBeforeClientOpenTicket`, `onAfterClientOpenTicket`, etc.). See the [0.7 to 0.8 upgrade guide](/maintenance/updating/0-7-to-0-8/#public-ticket-unification-083) for details.
{% /aside %}

## Product Hooks

### Service License

- `onBeforeServicelicenseReset`
- `onAfterServicelicenseReset`

## Using Hooks in Your Module

Define public static handlers in your module's `Service.php`. The `onAfterAdminOrderCreate` event passes the order ID in its parameters.

```php
class Service
{
    public static function onAfterAdminOrderCreate(\Box_Event $event): void
    {
        $orderId = $event->getParameters()['id'];
        error_log('New order created: ' . $orderId);
    }
}
```

## Troubleshooting Hook Discovery

FOSSBilling registers hooks when you activate a module and refreshes them during cron. After adding or renaming a handler in an active module, run cron once to register the change. See [cron troubleshooting](/maintenance/troubleshooting/#issues-with-cron) if scheduled tasks are overdue.
